    "13.5 Write property test for no raw sensitive value reaching a report file": {
      "status": "failed",
      "failingExample": "Property 22 / Requirement 8.10 violated. Two independent leaks found:\n\n(1) CSV renderer leaks raw client IP (and email) embedded in free-form title/detail.\n  payload=(ip='0.0.0.0', email='00@example.com', secret='00000000', ctrl='\\x00')\n  CSV file content: \"high,test.leak,activity from 0.0.0.0 for 00@example.com,observed 00@example.com using token=00000000 at 0.0.0.0,...\"\n  Root cause: file_csv._finding_to_row passes finding.title and finding.detail only through _secure_field (strip_control + csv_safe) with NO masking. Only metadata values are masked. The JSON renderer masks title/detail via _sanitize, so an IP/email in prose becomes 0.0.x.x / 0…@example.com there, but CSV writes them raw.\n\n(2) Both renderers leak a raw secret/token embedded in free-form prose or a non-credential-named field.\n  payload=(ip='0.0.0.0', email='00@example.com', secret='00000000', ctrl='\\x00')\n  JSON file content includes event field: \"user_agent\": \"agent 00000000\" (raw secret on disk). mask_secret('00000000') -> '00…00'.\n  Root cause: secrets are masked only when under a credential-named key (_SECRET_KEY_HINTS) or in a key=value assignment (_SECRET_ASSIGNMENT). A bare secret in prose / a non-credential field (e.g. user_agent) is not masked. Unlike IPs/emails, a secret has no intrinsic shape, so this case may need a spec clarification on how far the no-leak guarantee extends into free-form text.\n\nThe test is correct against the documented contract (Property 22: \"the text rendered to a report file does not contain the original unmasked value\"; Req 8.10: SHALL NOT write any raw unmasked value of the sensitive categories 7/8/9). Not weakening the assertion; reporting the leak.",
      "lastRunTimestamp": 1793745859062
    },
